---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const title = 'About HumanAverage';
const description =
  'An independent project that calculates percentiles from public health survey microdata, ' +
  'shows its working, and says plainly what it cannot know.';
---

<Base title={title} description={description} canonical="/about/">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>A small project with one rule</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        No anonymous “research team”. HumanAverage is an independent project run by one person,
        built on one rule: no number appears on this site unless it can be traced back to data.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow content">
      <h2>Why it exists</h2>
      <p>
        Search for “average height” and you get a number. It is usually correct, and it is
        almost useless — because you did not really want to know the average. You wanted to know
        where <em>you</em> stand.
      </p>
      <p>
        Answering that takes more than quoting a summary. It takes the individual measurements
        behind the summary, the statistical weights that make them represent a population, and
        the arithmetic to turn all of it into your position in the distribution. That is what
        this site does, and the <a href="/method/">method page</a> shows exactly how.
      </p>

      <h2>Who makes it</h2>
      <p>
        HumanAverage is published and maintained by Simeon as an independent project. There is
        no medical team, research institute or editorial department behind it. Where software or
        AI helps prepare the work, the publisher remains responsible for the final check, the
        choice of sources and the decision to publish.
      </p>

      <h2>Editorial principles</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We never invent a statistic. Every figure comes from a dataset we can point to.</li>
        <li>Percentiles are calculated from microdata, never copied from published averages.</li>
        <li>We show no percentile where no representative sample exists, however tempting.</li>
        <li>We separate our own calculation from results published by others.</li>
        <li>We describe what a comparison means, and what it does not.</li>
        <li>We correct demonstrable errors and say when the method was last checked.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How it is paid for</h2>
      <p>
        HumanAverage is free to use. Advertising may eventually help cover hosting and further
        development. It currently carries no advertising code, and adverts would never change a
        calculation or a conclusion.
      </p>

      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        If you can show that something here is wrong, that is genuinely useful and it will be
        fixed. Email <a href="mailto:firenature23@gmail.com">firenature23@gmail.com</a>. For a
        question about a specific result, mentioning your age, sex and the value you entered
        helps.
      </p>

      <div class="callout">
        <p>
          This site is an informational comparison. It is not medical advice, not a diagnosis,
          and not an assessment of your health.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
